Z||000000||BAM-BAM||06-21-2001||11:15 PM|||| I want to move forward with my swap. Here is the scenario as it is now.  I currently have the following.<P>1.) New 3.4L crate engine.<P>2.) West coast headers and cat.<P>3.) Borla cat back system<P>4.) 19# injectors (less than 30 miles)<P>5.) Poly cradle bushings<P>6.) West coast poly mounts<P>What's coming<BR>1.) Upper and middle intake<P>2.) Engine cradle<P>3.) Starter<P>4.)lower intake<P>What else do I need? I think I need to do something about the flexplate, right? Also, I would like to get a better oil pan, does it matter what year? 85-87 V6? I will be reusing most of my other accessories. I will be converting over to R-134 while I'm at it.<BR>If there is anything that I have missed, please inform me. I appriciate every bit of help that I get here. You all are the best.<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Knowledge is POWER!<BR>That is why the ignorant remain Weak!||||reg||5
