Z||000012||Black88GT||06-22-2001||08:26 PM||||After the starter holes its pretty much set (of course you have to add the Fiero intake to the 3.4 block/heads).  I had to buy some modified brackets from Ed Parks, but if I would have known what was involved I would have made them myself.  I am pretty sure though I needed to buy them anyway, something about '88s needed to use pre-88 A/C brackets or something. <P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff (AOL IM - FieroTT)<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif">     <BR><I>"Once you go black, you never go back..."</I><BR><I>"The Customer Can Have Any Color He Wants So Long As It's Black" </I> -Henry Ford||||reg||12
